Ryujinx shader translator, goto elimination: a break or continue that an earlier step of goto elimination put in
place (MoveOutward: "if (c) break;" where a goto leaves a loop) could end up inside a do-while that a later goto
creates around it (EncloseDoWhile, also through Lift). Gotos are eliminated last to first, so the exit of a loop is
handled before the gotos in its body; when one of those encloses the exit in a new loop, the break leaves only the new
loop and control falls back into the old one. If it was that loop's only exit, the shader never ends: the game A8, the light
loop of a family of material shaders (BRA back edge, CALL.REL.NOINC exit, a BRX switch inside whose cases jump to the
switch's end): the GPU was lost after the driver's timeout (AGENTS.md, artifact A8). Now a newly created do-while
checks what it encloses: a break or continue that is not inside a loop nested in it sets a flag and leaves the new
loop, and right after it "if (flag) { flag = false; break; }" (or continue) repeats the exit for the loop it was made
for (the flag is also cleared at the start of the function). Eliminate takes a function that declares the flags as locals
(structured-program-cfg-check.patch passes StructuredProgramContext.NewTemp). Checked with NXRT_HARNESS_CFG_CHECK
(translator/StructuredCfgCheck.cs). The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
